OL,3,ATories would prevent long-term jobless
OL,4,Aspending benefits on alcohol and
OL,5,Acigarettes
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe Conservatives have promised to
OL,8,Fprevent long-term jobless benefit
OL,9,Fclaimants from spending their welfare
OL,10,Fpayments on alcohol, cigarettes and
OL,11,Fgambling.
OL,13,FUnder the party's proposals, claimants
OL,14,Fwho have been unemployed for more than
OL,15,Fsix months would see their Universal
OL,16,FCredit cut by 30% if they have not
OL,17,Fpreviously paid enough into the system,
OL,18,Fdespite being able to work.
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/38
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11908
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1790240147
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ATories would prevent long-term jobless
OL,4,Aspending benefits on alcohol and
OL,5,Acigarettes
OL,6,
OL,7,FThis reduced rate would be paid onto a
OL,8,F"Back to Work" card, which would not
OL,9,Fallow cash withdrawals or spending on
OL,10,Fthese items.
OL,12,FThe Tories said the proposals were
OL,13,Fdesigned to encourage people back into
OL,14,Fwork and cut the soaring welfare bill
OL,15,Fbut Labour branded the scheme
OL,16,F"unworkable".
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/38
